You are performing scientific data-quality review for assay-transfer calibration.

The numerical tail only triggered review; do not prune mechanically from a cutoff. Decide
whether each value is a scientifically credible, quantitatively comparable measurement of
this bucket's endpoint. A value repeated faithfully in support text can still be unsuitable
because the source may contain a decimal or unit error, assay failure, saturation, unstable
calculation, or a result outside the meaningful range of the method.

Prune when the evidence more likely than not indicates a different quantity or endpoint,
wrong unit or scale, corrupt extraction, or a scientifically implausible or methodologically
out-of-domain value. You do not need proof of the intended correction. Keep a rare extreme
when it remains scientifically plausible for this endpoint and method. If the evidence is
genuinely balanced, keep with insufficient_evidence. Do not convert, repair, or reassign.

Pruning only excludes a record from assay-transfer calibration. It never rejects a bucket
and never deletes a row from the canonical or retrieval library.

Return one decision for every row ID under "Rows requiring a decision" and no decisions
